   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Regular forms",
     "texto": [
      "The starting point is the **eles** form of the pretérito perfeito and the final **-m** is removed, leaving the **-r**: **falaram** → **falar** (to speak), **comeram** → **comer** (to eat), **partiram** → **partir** (to leave).",
      "With **tu**: **falares**, **comeres**, **partires**. With **ele** / **você**: **falar**, **comer**, **partir**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Irregular forms",
     "texto": [
      "**ser / ir** → **for** (will be), **fores** (you will be), **forem** (they will be). **ter** → **tiver** (will have), **tiveres** (you will have). **fazer** → **fizer** (will do), **fizeres** (you will do). **estar** → **estiver** (will be).",
      "So: **Se for preciso** (if it is necessary)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "When it is used",
     "texto": [
      "With **quando** (when), **assim que** (as soon as), **se** (if): **Quando chegares, avisa-me** (when you arrive, let me know). **Se tiveres tempo, vem** (if you have time, come).",
      "What happens afterwards takes the present or the imperative."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
